Done. Read the recon notes (the actual file was hindsight-recon.md, not hindsight-plan.md), created worktree hindsight/init from master, wrote deepcli/_v1_hindsight.py into it, committed/pushed and opened the PR, then removed the worktree.

PR URL: https://github.com/timerloggedout-spec/termux-monorepo/pull/881

New file: deepcli/_v1_hindsight.py (~12 KB). Defines three async tool handlers — retain / recall / reflect — that POST to a remote Hindsight server via httpx, plus:
- HindsightClient: minimal async HTTP client with aretain/arecall/areflect, bearer-auth, configurable base_url / bank_id / timeout via HINDSIGHT_BASE_URL, HINDSIGHT_API_KEY, HINDSIGHT_BANK_ID, HINDSIGHT_TIMEOUT_S (defaults to http://localhost:8888 per recon).
- HindsightError for non-2xx / network failures.
- build_hindsight_tools() returning HindsightToolSpec entries (hindsight_retain, hindsight_recall, hindsight_reflect) with JSON schemas, ready for plugin registration in a later round.
No changes to deepagent.py; the module is self-contained and imports nothing from it.<parameter>
